            <ArticleTitle>TGF-β Gives an Air of Exclusivity to Alveolar Macrophages.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>807-809</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1074-7613(17)30482-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.immuni.2017.11.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tissue-resident macrophages shape the development and homeostasis of the organs that they colonize. Yu et al. (2017) demonstrate that, unique to the lung, the instructive cytokine TGF-β collaborates with GM-CSF to induce the master transcription factor PPARγ to drive alveolar macrophage differentiation and maintenance early in life.</AbstractText>
